WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室风云》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为您制作了这档《办公室风云》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室风云》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉您的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室风云》女士。

8
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.640
We're going to do this.
我们要开始啦。

9
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:30.600
This is so cool.
这太酷了。

10
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.060
We are hanging out talking about The Office.
我们正聚在一起聊《办公室风云》呢。

11
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:39.820
Jenna, who is the person you want to sit next to in any high school chemistry class, she is the note taker.
珍娜，她是那种你在高中化学课上最想坐在她旁边的人，她是做笔记的人。

12
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.240
You don't watch Game of Thrones, so you will miss this reference.
你不看《权力的游戏》，所以你会听不懂这个梗。

13
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.460
You would be like, Jenna Fisher, first of her name.
你会说，珍娜·费舍尔，其名第一人。

14
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.540
Keeper of the notes of the records.
记录笔记的守护者。

15
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.940
I don't watch Game of Thrones, but I appreciate that.
我不看《权力的游戏》，但我领会到了。

16
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.380
Okay, well, you would be keeper of the notes.
好吧，那你就是笔记守护者。

17
00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.380
And she has made some really great notes.
她做了非常棒的笔记。

18
00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.460
And we both went back and rewatched which episode, Jenna?
我们俩都回去重温了哪一集，珍娜？

19
00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.000
Today, we are discussing the basketball episode.
今天，我们要讨论的是篮球那一集。

20
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.680
This is Season 1, Episode 5.
这是第一季第五集。

21
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:05.580
Boo-boo, boo-boo!
呜呜，呜呜！

22
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.440
It was written and directed by Greg Daniels.
这一集由格雷格·丹尼尔斯编剧并执导。

23
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:08.920
That's right.
没错。

24
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.120
Should we give it a synopsis of the episode?
我们要不要介绍一下这一集的剧情梗概？

25
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.480
I know you want to, Jenna.
我知道你想的，珍娜。

26
00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:13.980
Keeper of the notes.
笔记守护者。

27
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.000
Keeper of the notes.
笔记守护者。

28
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:15.820
Do it, lady.
来吧，女士。

29
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:16.920
I wrote down a synopsis.
我写了一份剧情梗概。

30
00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.080
She did, y'all.
她真的写了，各位。

31
00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:18.920
She typed it out.
她把它打出来了。

32
00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:19.380
It is.
确实。

33
00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:20.020
I'm going to read it.
我要读一下。

34
00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:20.280
Okay.
好的。

35
00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:26.980
In this episode, Michael challenges the guys in the warehouse to a basketball game against the upstairs sales staff.
在这一集中，迈克尔向仓库里的男员工们发起挑战，要和楼上的销售人员打一场篮球赛。

36
00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:34.680
The warehouse workers, led by Daryl, want to make it a friendly game, but Michael insists there be a prize for their winner, or more accurately, a punishment for the losers.
由达里尔领导的仓库员工们本想让这成为一场友谊赛，但迈克尔坚持要给赢家设个奖品，或者更准确地说，给输家设个惩罚。

37
00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:40.680
Michael suggests the losers have to work on Saturday, and then he taunts Daryl with chicken sounds until Daryl agrees.
迈克尔提议输的一方周六要加班，然后他一直用学鸡叫来嘲讽达里尔，直到达里尔同意为止。

38
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:42.560
Correct.
没错。

39
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.280
But things will get more interesting in this episode.
但这一集里事情会变得更有趣。

40
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.560
That's not where it ends, Angela.
故事还没完呢，安吉拉。

41
00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:47.980
I know.
我知道。

42
00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.260
The drama does not end there.
戏剧性冲突还没结束。

43
00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.040
Here's another dun-dun-dun paragraph.
这里还有一段“当当当”的悬念。

44
00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:51.780
What do you got here?
你写了什么？

45
00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:55.360
Yes, things get more interesting because Pam's fiancée, Roy, works in the warehouse.
是的，事情变得更有趣了，因为帕姆的未婚夫罗伊就在仓库工作。

46
00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:55.980
Oh, snap.
噢，天哪。

47
00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:56.680
Yes.
是的。

48
00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:04.100
So, we find out that she is caught between her office crush, Jim, and her actual fiancée, Roy.
所以，我们发现她夹在办公室里的暗恋对象吉姆和她的未婚夫罗伊之间。

49
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.060
Who is she going to root for, upstairs or downstairs?
她会为谁加油呢，楼上还是楼下？

50
00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:06.840
I don't know.
我不知道。

51
00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.600
Let's start with some fast facts.
让我们先从一些速览事实开始。

52
00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:09.660
It is your favorite part.
这是你们最喜欢的部分。

53
00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:10.540
You know it is.
你们知道的。

54
00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:15.600
Fast fact number one, this was Greg Daniels' directorial debut of The Office.
速览事实第一条，这是格雷格·丹尼尔斯执导《办公室》的处女作。

55
00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.940
Not just any debut of directing, right?
不仅仅是某种执导处女作，对吧？

56
00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:18.480
Of all directing.
是所有执导经历中的第一次。

57
00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.720
So, not just of The Office, but his debut debut.
所以，不仅仅是《办公室》，而是他导演生涯的真正处女作。

58
00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:27.000
Now, he told me he had directed actors before for Voices on The Simpsons and King of the Hill.
他告诉我，他之前在《辛普森一家》和《乡巴佬希尔》中指导过配音演员。

59
00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:27.280
Right.
没错。

60
00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.440
He created King of the Hill for anyone who doesn't know that.
顺便提一下，不知道的人可以了解下，他是《乡巴佬希尔》的创作者。

61
00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.240
But this was his first time doing on-camera directing.
但这是他第一次进行现场执导。

62
00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.620
He would go on to direct 12 more episodes of The Office, but this was the firSt.
后来他又执导了12集《办公室》，但这一集是第一集。

63
00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:37.060
Yes.
是的。

64
00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:43.760
And I remember him showing up in his New Balance sneakers, his gray New Balance sneakers, and his khaki pants.
我记得他穿着新百伦运动鞋，那双灰色的新百伦，还有卡其裤就来了。

65
00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.480
Greg always wears anything he got for free.
格雷格总是穿任何他免费得到的东西。

66
00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.000
So, like, his shirt might have said King of the Hill.
所以，他的衬衫上可能印着《乡巴佬希尔》。

67
00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.840
His baseball hat might have said The Simpsons.
他的棒球帽上可能印着《辛普森一家》。

68
00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.940
Mindy Kaling used to joke he just wore all his swag all the time.
敏迪·卡灵常开玩笑说，他总是把所有周边产品穿在身上。

69
00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.640
But he showed up so giddy and excited.
但他出现时显得非常兴奋和激动。

70
00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:03.040
His enthusiasm and love for this show and this world and characters, it was just so contagious.
他对这部剧、这个世界和这些角色的热情与热爱，真的非常有感染力。

71
00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.400
I just loved it so much.
我太喜欢了。

72
00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.780
It made me excited.
这让我感到很兴奋。

73
00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.920
Fast fact number two, this is the episode where we introduce the character of Daryl.
速览事实第二条，这一集是我们引入达里尔这个角色的那一集。

74
00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:11.660
That's right.
没错。

75
00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:12.960
Played by Craig Robinson.
由克雷格·罗宾逊饰演。

76
00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:14.820
Now, we see him for the first time in The Alliance.
我们在《联盟》那一集中第一次见到他。

77
00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.420
He's watching Dwight bust out of the box.
他当时在看德怀特从盒子里钻出来。

78
00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.900
But this is the first time he speaks, and this is the first time we learn his character name.
但这是他第一次开口说话，也是我们第一次知道他的角色名字。

79
00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:22.200
Right.
没错。

80
00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.120
This establishes him as a character on the show.
这确立了他作为剧中角色的地位。

81
00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:33.200
Now, I was emailing with Allison Jones, our casting director, because I wanted to know, how did you find Craig Robinson?
我当时正在和我们的选角导演艾莉森·琼斯发邮件，因为我想知道，你是怎么发现克雷格·罗宾逊的？

82
00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.140
He is so amazing.
他太棒了。

83
00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:44.180
And we knew that if the show went on, that this was a character who was going to recur, but who wasn't in the first couple of episodes.
我们知道如果剧集继续下去，这个角色将会成为常驻，尽管他没有出现在最初的几集中。

84
00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:51.860
Greg had talked to me about how he was going to fill out the world of The Office, and we were going to really get to know some of the people down in the warehouse.
格雷格曾和我谈过他打算如何充实《办公室》的世界，我们要真正去了解仓库里的一些人。

85
00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:58.400
He was going to introduce this character of Daryl as being one of Roy's friends, that they work in the warehouse together.
他打算引入达里尔这个角色，作为罗伊的朋友，他们一起在仓库工作。

86
00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.460
And so, Allison had to cast this person who we knew was going to recur, like Roy.
所以，艾莉森必须选出这个我们知道会常驻的角色，就像罗伊一样。

87
00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:09.340
She told me that she had seen him on a TV show called Lucky that he did with John Corbett.
她告诉我，她是在一部叫《幸运》的电视剧里看到他的，那是他和约翰·科贝特一起演的。

88
00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:16.840
So, she said from there, she had cast him in some small roles on Arrested Development and Curb Your Enthusiasm, because she also cast those shows.
她说从那以后，她还在《发展受阻》和《抑制热情》中为他安排了一些小角色，因为她也负责那些剧的选角。

89
00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.820
And she brought him in to audition for The Office.
然后她带他来参加了《办公室》的试镜。

90
00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:22.360
She's the reason why Craig ended up on our show.
她就是克雷格最终出现在我们剧中的原因。

91
00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.140
And Craig was very sought after in comedy circles.
而且克雷格在喜剧圈非常抢手。

92
00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.640
Like, I feel like that was a really big get for us.
我觉得这对我们来说真的是一个很大的收获。

93
00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:28.280
Oh, for sure.
哦，当然。

94
00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:28.540
Yeah.
是的。

95
00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.260
I mean, he's a huge comedian.
我的意思是，他是一位伟大的喜剧演员。

96
00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.600
He's so funny and so talented.
他既风趣又有才华。

97
00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.020
And so nice.
而且人特别好。

98
00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:34.840
And so nice.
人特别好。

99
00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.300
Why was everybody on our show so nice?
为什么我们剧组里的每个人都那么好？

100
00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:45.480
I feel like they did us this wonderful service of casting really talented people, but who were all really nice to each other.
我觉得他们为我们做了一件美妙的事，选拔了非常有才华的人，而且他们彼此之间都非常友善。

101
00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.480
We were really lucky, because we've both worked on other shows since.
我们真的很幸运，因为此后我们俩都参与了其他节目的制作。

102
00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:49.920
Where it is not the case.
而其他节目并非如此。

103
00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:50.820
We were like, oh, wow.
我们当时的感觉就是，哇哦。

104
00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:52.700
We were really lucky.
我们真的很幸运。

105
00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.180
Really, really lucky.
真的，非常幸运。

106
00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.500
Okay, are you ready for our last fast fact?
好了，准备好迎接我们最后一个冷知识了吗？

107
00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:57.180
Yeah.
准备好了。

108
00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:03.280
In the very early moments of this episode, you see the boom microphone dip down into frame.
在这一集的开头，你可以看到收音杆麦克风垂进了画面里。

109
00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.160
Oh, look at you catching a little boom.
噢，你竟然还抓到了一个小收音杆。

110
00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:05.760
I did.
我确实抓到了。

111
00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.000
Now, normally, you would never allow this on television.
通常情况下，电视节目是绝对不允许出现这种情况的。

112
00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:08.480
Right.
没错。

113
00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.800
But on our show, this was considered gold.
但在我们的节目里，这被视为珍宝。

114
00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.620
We kept this stuff in.
我们把这些镜头保留了下来。

115
00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.240
Like, you never not used a take that was funny.
比如，只要是好笑的镜头，我们就绝不会弃用。

116
00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:16.020
Right.
没错。

117
00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:22.440
Just because you saw the boom microphone or anything, any quote-unquote mistake that would normally get cut out of another show.
哪怕你看到了收音杆，或者任何在其他节目里通常会被剪掉的所谓“失误”。

118
00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:22.900
Right.
没错。

119
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:23.740
We used it.
我们都用了。

120
00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.760
Because you want it to feel like the documentary.
因为我们要让它感觉像是一部纪录片。

121
00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.060
Like an authentic documentary.
就像一部真实的纪录片。

122
00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:27.240
Right.
没错。

123
00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.140
This was really important.
这一点非常重要。

124
00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:30.120
So, I thought that was kind of a cool little thing.
所以我认为这是一个很酷的小细节。

125
00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:30.960
That is cool.
确实很酷。

126
00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.400
Our boom operator was named Nick Carbone.
我们的收音师名叫尼克·卡博内。

127
00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:33.780
Yeah.
没错。

128
00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:39.320
And one of my favorite things is when sometimes he would get the boom in the shot, we would yell, you got Carbone.
我最喜欢的一件事是，有时当他把收音杆拍进画面里时，我们会大喊：你被卡博内了。

129
00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:40.080
Carbone.
卡博内。

130
00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:40.980
You got Carbone.
你被卡博内了。

131
00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:46.260
And then we also started making up a song called Boom Shadow, Boom Shadow.
后来我们还编了一首歌，叫《收音杆阴影，收音杆阴影》。

132
00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.280
Listen, young kids, Google it.
听着，年轻人们，去谷歌搜一下吧。

133
00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.240
That is an old song.
那是一首老歌了。

134
00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.400
Angela, I have to share something else about Nick Carbone, our sound guy.
安吉拉，关于我们的录音师尼克·卡博内，我还有件事要分享。

135
00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:54.680
Okay.
好啊。

136
00:05:54.880 --> 00:06:00.700
So, Nick Carbone put a microphone on me every day for nine years.
尼克·卡博内九年来每天都给我别麦克风。

137
00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:01.240
Yes, he did.
没错，确实如此。

138
00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.020
It's a very intimate thing to mic an actor.
给演员别麦克风是一件非常私密的事情。

139
00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.420
Oftentimes, you know, I was in that pencil skirt.
通常，你知道，我穿着那种铅笔裙。

140
00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:07.840
Yeah.
没错。

141
00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:14.840
And if I was standing up, we would sometimes have to put a leg wrap around my upper thigh to hide the microphone pack.
如果我站着，有时我们得在大腿上缠上绑带，把麦克风发射器藏起来。

142
00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:22.620
And then very delicately weave a microphone wire through underneath my bra, up my blouse.
然后还要非常小心地把麦克风线从文胸下面穿过去，再一直向上穿过衬衫。

143
00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:25.520
And Nick Carbone was the person who did this every day.
而尼克·卡博内就是每天做这件事的人。

144
00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:26.640
For me, too.
我也是。

145
